{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine the graph of \\( y = f(2x + 1) \\), we need to understand the transformations applied to the original function \\( y = f(x) \\).\n\n1. **Horizontal Compression and Shift**:\n   - The function \\( y = f(2x + 1) \\) involves two transformations:\n     - A horizontal compression by a factor of 2 (because of \\( 2x \\)).\n     - A horizontal shift to the left by 1/2 unit (because of the \\( +1 \\) inside the function).\n\n2. **Horizontal Compression**:\n   - A horizontal compression by a factor of 2 means that every \\( x \\)-coordinate of the points on the graph of \\( y = f(x) \\) is halved. For example, if \\( (a, b) \\) is a point on \\( y = f(x) \\), then \\( (a/2, b) \\) will be a point on \\( y = f(2x) \\).\n\n3. **Horizontal Shift**:\n   - A shift to the left by 1/2 unit means that every \\( x \\)-coordinate of the points on the graph of \\( y = f(2x) \\) is decreased by 1/2. For example, if \\( (a/2, b) \\) is a point on \\( y = f(2x) \\), then \\( (a/2 - 1/2, b) \\) will be a point on \\( y = f(2x + 1) \\).\n\n","prefix_end":998,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,279,4771,315,17767,379,284,282,7,17,87,488,220,16,8,1124,701,582,1184,311,3535,279,52970,9251,311,279,4024,729,17767,379,284,282,2075,8,1124,3593,16,13,3070,15837,66161,323,26510,334,510,256,481,576,729,17767,379,284,282,7,17,87,488,220,16,8,1124,8,17601,1378,52970,510,257,481,362,16202,25111,553,264,8168,315,220,17,320,27653,315,17767,220,17,87,1124,39467,257,481,362,16202,6407,311,279,2115,553,220,16,14,17,4982,320,27653,315,279,17767,488,16,1124,8,4766,279,729,3593,17,13,3070,15837,66161,334,510,256,481,362,16202,25111,553,264,8168,315,220,17,3363,429,1449,17767,856,1124,7287,62526,315,279,3501,389,279,4771,315,17767,379,284,282,2075,8,1124,8,374,14761,2066,13,1752,3110,11,421,17767,320,64,11,293,8,1124,8,374,264,1459,389,